From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: GammaOS's azahar-nano commits of 2026-10-20

Three commits GammaOS made to azahar-nano after the state patch 000 holds
(https://github.com/TheGammaSqueeze/GammaOSNextDistribution-14, path
gammaos/emulators/azahar-nano):

- 43f1f504258: when the emulator falls more than two periods behind, the
  frame goes on the schedule's next slot instead of restarting the schedule
  from now, so the schedule keeps its offset against vblank.
- cfd0c22df98, afb19857d2c: the right-eye skip (patch 006 turns it on) drops
  only draws with a viewport of the left eye's pass. Super Mario 3D Land draws
  its bottom screen into the eyes' target between the eyes, and the skip took
  those draws for the right eye: the bottom screen flashed blue.

On the RG52 Mini, Super Mario 3D Land from its savestate, 60 s: 58.42 and
58.68 fps against 58.47 and 58.62 without them, with the same profile.

